{"id": "EUVD-2026-97046", "enisaUuid": "b6c46fbc-9e3e-370e-a667-e6d660382cf5", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the batchEditUsers handler of SysUserController that allows any authenticated user to edit user department assignments. Low-privileged attackers can send PUT requests to /sys/user/batchEditUsers with arbitrary user and department ids to move users, including administrators, between departments and overwrite positions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:33:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:59:10", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_user_batch_edit.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysUserController.java#L1955-L1967", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-user-batcheditusers"], "aliases": ["GHSA-px44-73hg-cqm3", "CVE-2026-108872"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "39cd577a-030a-3237-bfc0-30b16800d528", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "172801f5-2a44-3378-8a63-98ef5928874a", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}